{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "83a40b0b-93ff-4d0b-8da0-1b723f934217",
    "name": "Quipu Knowledge Graph Service",
    "description": "Complete REST API collection for the Quipu Knowledge Graph Service microservice (port 3034). Single access point for knowledge-graph data: proxies Cypher queries, namespace lifecycle, shape ingestion, and watchers to the external Synapse engine; talks to Neo4j and Milvus directly; and integrates with llm-service (Smart LLM) and application-service (schema metadata).\n\nCollection variables:\n- {{baseUrl}}  — default http://localhost:3034\n- {{token}}    — bearer/JWT-like token sent as Authorization header (forwarded downstream, not validated locally)\n- {{tenantId}} — tenant identifier (X-Tenant-ID header)\n\nNotes:\n- Endpoints in '02 — Metadata' produce application/vnd.quipu.rdf.meta-data+json;version=1.0.0; '03 — Smart LLM' uses application/vnd.quipu.llm-client+json;version=1.0.0 (generate-answer) and text/vnd.quipu.llm-client+plain;version=1.0.0 (generate-query); '05 — Vector Client' uses application/vnd.quipu.vector-client+json;version=1.0.0.\n- Cypher time-travel (`atTime`, epoch millis) is a JSON BODY field on POST /synapse/query, not a query string parameter.\n- '/synapse/watchers/**' and most of '/synapse/namespace/**' proxy Synapse verbatim — response bodies/status codes are relayed from the external Synapse engine.\n- A STOMP/SockJS chat endpoint exists at /chat (WebSocketConfig) but is NOT a standard REST call — Postman's WebSocket support does not speak STOMP frames natively; it requires a STOMP-aware client (e.g. @stomp/stompjs) and is out of scope for this collection.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "56383100",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/56383100-83a40b0b-93ff-4d0b-8da0-1b723f934217?source=collection_link"
  },
